Build this: a kinetic-typography loop on white paper, timed at 30fps over a 57-tick seamless cycle (1.9s): a five-word sentence types itself in word by word, one key word explodes into colourful scribble strokes, and everything leaves the frame. TYPE-IN (ticks 0-14): words arrive every 3 ticks; each lands OVERSIZED (2.0x for the first word, which arrives alone and centred; 1.35x for the rest) and slightly blurred, shrinking + sharpening into place with a per-tick follower (retain 0.7 of the excess per tick). Later words also START ~1em RIGHT of their slot and slide in as they sharpen. The LAST word is the pun: it arrives genuinely out of focus (blur ~9px at a 48px em) and takes 8 ticks to resolve. THE LINE'S GLIDE IS MEASURED, NOT MODELLED: when the second word arrives the whole line moves toward its FINAL layout position (nearly home 2 ticks before the last word lands), OVERSHOOTS by ~9-10% and eases back over ~12 ticks — encode that trajectory as a lookup table, not an exponential follower (a follower misses both the fast middle and the overshoot). Implement the blur as a progressive downscale/upscale chain (halve 1-3 times, then double back up, bilinear each step) — one big jump reads as mosaic, not blur. HOLD (15-25), then HEAT-UP (26-34): the burst word's letters tint from ink toward per-letter DUSTY PASTELS (tan / dusty pink / rose / mauve, all near L=0.68 — the word LIGHTENS as it heats) on an ease-out ramp, then SHAKE (30-43): per-letter jitter (rotation to ~13deg, y to ~6px, a ~5Hz buzz plus slow per-letter drifts apart) with a quadratic amplitude envelope. BURST (44-51): two things at once. (1) The word's final jittered state is captured to an offscreen sprite and SLICED into per-letter horizontal ribbons (7 rows) that rain down-and-out, rows accelerating ~1.22x/tick, outer rows faster, letters spreading apart horizontally. (2) HATCH GROUPS of drawn strokes (4-7 parallel tapered dashes with round caps, drawn as two stroke segments — thin tail half, full-width head half — with a slight per-dash bend) launch from the word's edges along measured keyframe paths, LENGTHS GROWING ~10x over eight ticks, and — the signature — each group's HUE SLIDES ALONG THE SPECTRUM in flight (purple crosses into blue, orange warms into gold); give each dash a linear gradient along its length. Meanwhile the surviving words ZOOM about the burst word's centre (S = 1 + 0.35*u^1.8 over 8 ticks), get an extra outward THROW (~17px by the zoom's end on a u^2.5 curve, then multiplying 1.9x/tick), and FADE OUT while accelerating so they are gone within a tick of full strength. FINALE (51-55): the small hatches hand over to a few OVERSIZED single strokes crossing the emptying frame (a green hook out the top-left, a thick blue bar sweeping right, a warm diagonal out the bottom-left), all clear by tick 55; two BLANK ticks close the loop. All jitter comes from one seeded PRNG rolled at init so the loop plays identically every time. Canvas 2D, framework-free engine + a rAF loop that only redraws when the 30fps tick changes; DPR-capped at 2; pauses offscreen / hidden / during route transitions; one static mid-burst frame under reduced motion.

The complete, self-contained implementation follows, one file per block. It is framework-agnostic core logic — wire it into your own component and mount it on an element.

